the eye, such as uveitis

481
00:26:33,210 --> 00:26:36,370
or episcleritis. There's
also joint inflammation

482
00:26:36,370 --> 00:26:38,970
and joint involvement.
And this is not only

483
00:26:38,970 --> 00:26:41,800
seen as arthritis, but a
lot of the seronegative

484
00:26:42,650 --> 00:26:44,570
spondyloarthropathies.
And there's also

485
00:26:44,570 --> 00:26:47,360
oral ulcers called
apthysstomatitis.

486
00:26:47,770 --> 00:26:50,210
Now there's also a
common rash that's

487
00:26:50,210 --> 00:26:53,070
described, pyoderma
gangrenosum, which really is

488
00:26:53,070 --> 00:26:56,150
tissue necrosis leading
to quite deep ulcers,

489
00:26:56,150 --> 00:26:58,170
and it's typically
present in the legs.

490
00:26:58,870 --> 00:27:03,750
And you can also develop
primary sclerosing cholangitis,

491
00:27:03,750 --> 00:27:06,290
not the disease that we
had talked about earlier,

492
00:27:06,290 --> 00:27:09,710
primary biliary cholangitis,
but both of these

493
00:27:09,710 --> 00:27:13,910
disease processes are associated
actually with P. ANCA,

494
00:27:13,910 --> 00:27:16,530
which we'll be discussing
briefly on our next slide.

495
00:27:19,650 --> 00:27:23,410
In regards to the diagnosis
of ulcerative colitis,

496
00:27:23,410 --> 00:27:28,120
what we'll have is an increase
in the ESR or erythrocyte

497
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:30,750
sedimentation rate kind
of pointing to a sign of

498
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:34,410
inflammation as well as a
decreased hemoglobin and

499
00:27:34,410 --> 00:27:37,550
hematocrit pointing to that
anemia picture which we briefly

500
00:27:37,550 --> 00:27:41,090
mentioned below. What
we'll also find is positive

501
00:27:41,090 --> 00:27:46,110
P-ANCA which is perinuclear
antineutrophilic cytoplasmic

502
00:27:46,110 --> 00:27:48,850
antibodies and these are
targeted specifically

503
00:27:48,850 --> 00:27:52,610
against myeloperoxidase,
which is found in neutrophils.

504
00:27:52,950 --> 00:27:56,050
So pianka is not specific
to just ulcerative

505
00:27:56,050 --> 00:27:58,110
colitis, but it's
also seen in other

506
00:27:58,110 --> 00:28:00,810
microscopic polyangitis
type diseases,

507
00:28:00,990 --> 00:28:04,150
Churk-Strauss syndrome.
You'll hear about it with

508
00:28:04,150 --> 00:28:07,130
primary sclerosing
cholangitis, as we mentioned on

509
00:28:07,130 --> 00:28:10,710
the slide prior. In terms
of other testing, it's

510
00:28:10,710 --> 00:28:13,670
important to send stool
bacterial cultures in order to

511
00:28:13,670 --> 00:28:17,070
rule out other causes of
****** diarrhea that mimic

512
00:28:17,070 --> 00:28:20,030
signs and symptoms of
ulcerative colitis, such as

513
00:28:20,030 --> 00:28:24,130
salmonella, shigella, we
talk about E. coli as well.

514
00:28:24,390 --> 00:28:28,330
In terms of further testing,
if we were to do a barium

515
00:28:28,330 --> 00:28:31,470
*****, there's actually a
picture that's shown here.

516
00:28:31,470 --> 00:28:34,510
What we'll find is when we
do a double contrast barium

517
00:28:34,510 --> 00:28:37,970
*****, it leads to what's
called a lead pipe sign,

518
00:28:37,970 --> 00:28:41,390
and this is because there's
