520
00:28:45,110 --> 00:28:47,830
Furthermore, you can
do endoscopic biopsy

521
00:28:47,830 --> 00:28:49,890
to also demonstrate
the findings of

522
00:28:49,890 --> 00:28:52,870
ulcerative colitis as
well as colonoscopy.

523
00:28:53,170 --> 00:28:56,690
In terms of just the
gross morphology, what

524
00:28:56,690 --> 00:28:58,650
you'll find, and this
is a common distinction

525
00:28:58,650 --> 00:29:00,870
between ulcerative
colitis and Crohn's

526
00:29:00,870 --> 00:29:03,670
disease, is that you'll
have with ulcerative

527
00:29:03,670 --> 00:29:07,550
colitis mucosal and
submucosal inflammation.

528
00:29:07,710 --> 00:29:10,850
The mucosa is also friable
and there's variable

529
00:29:10,850 --> 00:29:13,250
depth of ulcerations.
However, with

530
00:29:13,250 --> 00:29:16,530
ulcerative colitis, this
is not transmural. It is

531
00:29:16,530 --> 00:29:18,880
not going through the
intestine completely.

532
00:29:19,110 --> 00:29:21,810
There's also
pseudopolyp formation.

533
00:29:22,130 --> 00:29:26,130
Because this is not
transmural, we also don't see

534
00:29:26,130 --> 00:29:28,970
