most cases of ulcerative

535
00:29:28,970 --> 00:29:32,930
colitis. And on microscopy,
ulcerative colitis is

536
00:29:32,930 --> 00:29:35,810
typically described as
having crypt abscesses and

537
00:29:35,810 --> 00:29:39,130
ulcers. However, there is
no granuloma formation.

538
00:29:39,590 --> 00:29:42,990
When looking at the treatment
of ulcerative colitis,

539
00:29:42,990 --> 00:29:48,190
we have 5-ASA or aminosalicylic
acid preparations as

540
00:29:48,190 --> 00:29:50,810
well as things like
sulfasalazine or mechanisms and

541
00:29:50,810 --> 00:29:54,050
medications such as
sulfasalazine. And what that is is

542
00:29:54,050 --> 00:29:57,720
really it's actually a combination
of the 5-aminosalicylic

543
00:29:57,720 --> 00:30:01,630
acid as well as sulfapyridine.
So this is not only

544
00:30:01,630 --> 00:30:05,050
an NSAID type mechanism,
but also an antibacterial.

545
00:30:05,340 --> 00:30:08,070
And so what happens is a
lot of these medications

546
00:30:08,070 --> 00:30:11,070
are NSAIDs or non
-steroidal anti-inflammatory

547
00:30:11,070 --> 00:30:14,090
drugs that are specifically
metabolized in the

548
00:30:14,090 --> 00:30:16,710
colon. And so these are
useful in these disease

549
00:30:16,710 --> 00:30:19,530
processes as they
primarily affect the colon.

550
00:30:19,790 --> 00:30:22,370
There's also medications
that you'll hear about,

551
00:30:22,370 --> 00:30:25,440
like 6-mercaptopurine,
and this is a purine

552
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:28,790
antimetabolite. So this
inhibits the synthesis of DNA

553
00:30:28,790 --> 00:30:32,970
and RNA, and in this case,
it actually prohibits

554
00:30:32,970 --> 00:30:35,650
and inhibits the synthesis
of the cells that cause

555
00:30:35,650 --> 00:30:39,290
the inflammatory process
in ulcerative colitis.

556
00:30:39,470 --> 00:30:43,130
There's also some antibody
-type medication, such as

557
00:30:43,130 --> 00:30:45,650
infliximab, and that's
also used to treat the

558
00:30:45,650 --> 00:30:49,290
spondyloarthropathies associated
with ulcerative colitis,

559
00:30:49,290 --> 00:30:52,530
and its mechanism is a
tumor necrosis factor alpha

560
00:30:52,530 --> 00:30:56,290
inhibitor. In very severe
disease, I've seen this before

561
00:30:56,290 --> 00:30:59,490
as well, you'll see colectomies
performed on patients,

562
00:30:59,490 --> 00:31:02,330
especially in those who
have diseases that are

563
00:31:02,330 --> 00:31:05,350
refractory to any of the
treatments available. If

564
00:31:05,350 --> 00:31:08,890
there's signs and stigmata
of dysplasia or cancer and

565
00:31:08,890 --> 00:31:12,130
carcinoma, we'll often see
colectomy being performed.

566
00:31:15,690 --> 00:31:19,390
Now that we've discussed
many of the diseases of the

567
00:31:19,390 --> 00:31:23,130
gastrointestinal tract and
gastrointestinal system,

568
00:31:23,130 --> 00:31:25,370
we'll take a second here
to rehearse and practice

569
00:31:25,370 --> 00:31:29,210
with the case. So here we
have a 22-year-old female

570
00:31:29,210 --> 00:31:32,350
presenting to the clinic
with a chief complaint of

571
00:31:32,350 --> 00:31:36,350
****** diarrhea and what she
describes to be cold sores

572
00:31:36,350 --> 00:31:39,230
at the corners of her
lips that have not healed.

573
00:31:39,390 --> 00:31:43,030
She does report recent
camping trip but denies any

574
00:31:43,030 --> 00:31:46,410
fevers or chills? Her labs
are demonstrated below.

575
00:31:46,790 --> 00:31:50,130
What is the potential
disease process at hand?

576
00:31:50,830 --> 00:31:53,930
So take a second to think
about what's going on here.

