children but also in adults

615
00:33:51,290 --> 00:33:54,190
and some of the mechanisms
make them particularly

616
00:33:54,190 --> 00:33:57,750
unique in comparison to
the other kidney diseases.

617
00:34:01,130 --> 00:34:04,110
The first disease process
that we'll be talking

618
00:34:04,110 --> 00:34:07,220
about is post-streptococcal
glomerulonephritis,

619
00:34:07,220 --> 00:34:11,880
and in this case, the
mechanism at play is IgG,

620
00:34:11,930 --> 00:34:17,170
IgM, and C3-mediated with
complex and deposition on

621
00:34:17,170 --> 00:34:21,290
glomerular basement membranes
and mesangium. In this

622
00:34:21,290 --> 00:34:24,390
case, it's a very specific
type of pathogenesis called

623
00:34:24,390 --> 00:34:27,370
molecular mimicry, and
in this case, we're also

624
00:34:27,370 --> 00:34:30,590
dealing with group A strep
or strep pharyngitis also

625
00:34:30,590 --> 00:34:35,290
causing impetigo, leading to
be the nephrodogenic agent.

626
00:34:35,650 --> 00:34:38,770
Specifically, the M protein
is actually what's known

627
00:34:38,770 --> 00:34:41,750
as the virulence factor
in this disease process.

628
00:34:41,810 --> 00:34:45,690
What we'll see is that
it's also organ specific,

629
00:34:45,770 --> 00:34:48,830
specifically with the renal
glomerular basement membrane

630
00:34:48,830 --> 00:34:51,510
and the mesangium.
However, just like all the

631
00:34:51,510 --> 00:34:55,770
other processes, there are
systemic signs and stigmata.

632
00:34:55,770 --> 00:34:58,690
So what we'll see oftentimes
in children is that

633
00:34:58,690 --> 00:35:01,670
the process is actually
asymptomatic. However, it

634
00:35:01,670 --> 00:35:04,630
does go upwards to leading
to a nephrotic syndrome.

635
00:35:05,010 --> 00:35:07,950
Commonly, it's seen in
children, typically about

636
00:35:07,950 --> 00:35:11,430
