643
00:35:31,290 --> 00:35:35,190
In terms of the diagnosis
of post-treptococcal

644
00:35:35,210 --> 00:35:38,870
glomerulonephritis, keep in
mind the disease process uses

645
00:35:38,870 --> 00:35:43,950
IgM, IgG, and C3, and we're
using these to form complex

646
00:35:43,950 --> 00:35:47,570
deposition on your glomerular
basement membrane. So

647
00:35:47,570 --> 00:35:50,870
if we're testing for C3,
it's being used up on these

648
00:35:50,870 --> 00:35:53,810
depositions, and so you'll
actually have low levels

649
00:35:53,810 --> 00:35:58,630
of C3. On top of that, we
can test for ASO titers or

650
00:35:58,890 --> 00:36:01,450
