of the antigen-antibody

657
00:36:19,350 --> 00:36:22,310
complex in the glomerular
basement membrane.

658
00:36:22,680 --> 00:36:25,540
On top of this, with
electron microscopy,

659
00:36:25,670 --> 00:36:28,450
you might also see
findings of sub-epithelial

660
00:36:28,450 --> 00:36:30,770
immune complex
depositions consistent

661
00:36:30,770 --> 00:36:32,860
with what we had seen
and discussed before.

662
00:36:33,990 --> 00:36:35,790
In terms of our treatments,

663
00:36:35,790 --> 00:36:38,490
we're talking about
antihypertensives because we

664
00:36:38,490 --> 00:36:41,030
were mentioning previously
that one of the signs of

665
00:36:41,030 --> 00:36:44,290
this disease process is
hypertension, as well as

666
00:36:44,290 --> 00:36:46,890
antibiotics, because keep
in mind this is caused

667
00:36:46,890 --> 00:36:50,170
by a group A strep infection.
And for the nephrotic

668
00:36:50,170 --> 00:36:52,590
syndrome sequelae, we
can talk about sodium

669
00:36:52,590 --> 00:36:55,990
restriction and diuretics
and predominantly supportive

670
00:36:55,990 --> 00:36:59,850
care. Now, I want to make
one point clear is that

671
00:36:59,850 --> 00:37:04,220
in terms of antibiotics,
this does not prevent

672
00:37:04,220 --> 00:37:09,630
the progression of group
A strep to PSGN. However,

673
00:37:09,750 --> 00:37:12,890
the administration of
antibiotics like penicillin

674
00:37:12,890 --> 00:37:17,290
G can prevent the nephrodogenic
strain from spreading

675
00:37:17,290 --> 00:37:19,890
from one person to
another. So it's not

676
00:37:19,890 --> 00:37:23,430
necessarily to halt the
progression from group A strep

677
00:37:23,430 --> 00:37:26,910
to this kidney malfunction.
However, it can help in

678
00:37:26,910 --> 00:37:30,130
stopping the spread from
one person to the next.

679
00:37:32,390 --> 00:37:36,030
Next, we'll be discussing
Goodpasture syndrome. And in

680
00:37:36,030 --> 00:37:40,210
this case, the mechanism
of action is IgG-mediated

681
00:37:40,210 --> 00:37:43,370
autoantibodies against the
intrinsic antigen of the

682
00:37:43,370 --> 00:37:47,910
glomerulobasement membrane.
So there are some genetic

683
00:37:47,910 --> 00:37:53,390
associations in this case,
specifically with HLA-DR2. However,

684
00:37:53,390 --> 00:37:56,990
commonly described is a
finding of an upper respiratory

685
00:37:56,990 --> 00:38:01,130
infection prior to the
presentation of Goodpasture

686
00:38:01,130 --> 00:38:04,450
syndrome or the presentations
of pulmonary hemorrhage

687
00:38:04,450 --> 00:38:08,490
leading to hemoptysis or a
cough with blood, rapidly

688
00:38:08,490 --> 00:38:11,230
