also looking for findings

696
00:38:38,650 --> 00:38:41,550
in other areas. As we
mentioned hematuria and

697
00:38:41,550 --> 00:38:45,310
hemoptysis, you'll also see
chest x-ray findings consistent

698
00:38:45,310 --> 00:38:48,050
with pulmonary infiltrates.
And if you were to

699
00:38:48,050 --> 00:38:51,110
proceed with immunofluorescence
microscopy, you'll

700
00:38:51,110 --> 00:38:54,050
find a linear pattern because
this follows the pattern

701
00:38:54,050 --> 00:38:57,170
of the membranes such as
the alveolar membrane.

702
00:38:57,340 --> 00:38:59,210
In terms of the treatment,

703
00:38:59,330 --> 00:39:01,970
The three treatment
modalities mentioned are

704
00:39:01,970 --> 00:39:04,130
corticosteroids, which
is consistent with many

705
00:39:04,130 --> 00:39:06,950
of the autoimmune processes
we've discussed, as

706
00:39:06,950 --> 00:39:09,220
well as cyclophosphamide
and plasmapheresis.

707
00:39:11,450 --> 00:39:14,630
Lastly, we're finally in
the home stretch. We'll

708
00:39:14,630 --> 00:39:17,610
briefly discuss a few of the
autoimmune diseases of the

709
00:39:17,610 --> 00:39:20,630
skin, and there are a few
key words and pictures that

710
00:39:20,630 --> 00:39:23,410
you'll see commonly presented
in many of the situations

711
00:39:23,410 --> 00:39:26,470
you'll come across, whether
it be on the boards,

712
00:39:26,470 --> 00:39:29,290
your comats, or in clinical
practice, and we'll try

713
00:39:29,290 --> 00:39:31,610
to highlight those as we
go through the discussion.

714
00:39:33,970 --> 00:39:37,910
The first disease process that
we'll mention is pemphigus

715
00:39:37,910 --> 00:39:41,070
vulgaris, in which case
the mechanism of action

716
00:39:41,070 --> 00:39:46,430
is IgG autoantibodies against
desmoglion 1 and or the

717
00:39:46,430 --> 00:39:50,750
inclusion and involvement
of desmoglion 3. And these

718
00:39:50,750 --> 00:39:53,870
proteins or desmosomes, what
they're in charge of doing

719
00:39:53,870 --> 00:39:57,290
and maintain is the connection
between keratinocytes

720
00:39:57,290 --> 00:40:00,890
in reference to the stratum
spinosum layer. And so

721
00:40:00,890 --> 00:40:04,170
what we'll have is there's
mucosal and possibly the

722
00:40:04,170 --> 00:40:07,390
involvement of the cutaneous
epithelial cell junctions.

723
00:40:07,710 --> 00:40:10,610
Specifically, Desmoglion
3 alone is more

724
00:40:10,610 --> 00:40:13,010
associated with mucosal
disease, while the

725
00:40:13,010 --> 00:40:16,370
presence of Desmoglion
1 and 3 involvement is

726
00:40:16,370 --> 00:40:19,150
more of a mucocutaneous
disease presentation.

727
00:40:19,390 --> 00:40:22,470
In terms of the signs
and symptoms, commonly,

728
00:40:22,470 --> 00:40:26,610
commonly described is a
positive Nikolsky sign. In this

729
00:40:26,610 --> 00:40:29,530
case, with a positive
Nikolsky sign, when the

730
00:40:29,530 --> 00:40:32,530
bullae that are formed,
these mucocutaneous or

731
00:40:32,530 --> 00:40:36,370
cutaneous eruptions are
formed, these bullae, the top

732
00:40:36,370 --> 00:40:39,030
layers of the skin, when
they're slightly touched,

733
00:40:39,030 --> 00:40:41,410
they slough or they slip
apart from the lower

734
00:40:41,410 --> 00:40:44,790
layers. This actually
differentiates the disease from

735
00:40:44,790 --> 00:40:46,810
a different disease
process called bullous

736
00:40:46,810 --> 00:40:50,050
pemphigoid. In that case,
when you actually touch the

737
00:40:50,050 --> 00:40:53,030
bullae, they're firm and
are not able to separate.

738
00:40:53,190 --> 00:40:55,910
So very important to
know the difference

739
00:40:55,910 --> 00:40:58,830
between the two with the
positive Nikolsky sign.

740
00:41:01,270 --> 00:41:05,350
In terms of diagnosis of
pemphigus vulgaris, there's

741
00:41:05,350 --> 00:41:08,390
a few different modalities
that we can use. Keep in

742
00:41:08,390 --> 00:41:11,590
mind, the entire mechanism
of all of these are the

743
00:41:11,590 --> 00:41:14,610
idea that there's deposition
of the anti-desmoglian

744
00:41:14,610 --> 00:41:18,870
antibodies, specifically
against Desmoglian 1 and

745
00:41:18,870 --> 00:41:23,070
Desmoglian 3. So if we were
to do light microscopy, the

746
00:41:23,070 --> 00:41:25,940
process that you might see
is called acantholysis.

747
00:41:26,390 --> 00:41:29,110
Sometimes this will be
described differently, such

748
00:41:29,110 --> 00:41:32,090
as in a row of tombstones.
And the reason this

749
00:41:32,090 --> 00:41:33,930
happens is because, keep
in mind, when you're

750
00:41:33,930 --> 00:41:36,950
sloughing off the skin,
it's really just the top

751
00:41:36,950 --> 00:41:39,450
layer that's coming off
that you're pulling off.

752
00:41:39,450 --> 00:41:42,290
And so the basement
membrane is still intact. So

753
00:41:42,290 --> 00:41:44,770
when you pull off this
top layer from the bottom,

754
00:41:44,770 --> 00:41:47,890
what appears to be shown
is a tombstone pattern.

755
00:41:48,010 --> 00:41:50,890
On top of that you can
also do what's called

756
00:41:50,890 --> 00:41:54,410
immunofluorescence leading to
a reticular pattern. Sometimes

757
00:41:54,410 --> 00:41:57,070
people will call this a lacy
pattern and occasionally

758
00:41:57,070 --> 00:42:00,630
I've seen it called a fishnet
pattern as well. So there's

759
00:42:00,630 --> 00:42:02,350
definitely a few different
ways that this can be

760
00:42:02,350 --> 00:42:05,810
described. In terms of the
treatment primarily we'll

761
00:42:05,810 --> 00:42:08,690
use corticosteroids but
the other mechanism and the

762
00:42:08,690 --> 00:42:11,630
other treatment that you'll
see is rituximab. So this is

763
00:42:11,630 --> 00:42:14,710
actually a chemotherapeutic
or anti-tumor medication,

764
00:42:14,710 --> 00:42:17,350
and it's chimeric, meaning
it still has some animal

765
00:42:17,350 --> 00:42:20,670
protein fragments. It's a
monoclonal antibody that

766
00:42:20,670 --> 00:42:24,930
selectively targets CD20,
which is found on B-cells. And

767
00:42:24,930 --> 00:42:28,150
so you'll activate a complement
-dependent cytotoxicity

768
00:42:28,150 --> 00:42:32,170
on these B-cells to lead
to apoptosis. So those are

769
00:42:32,170 --> 00:42:35,130
the treatments and diagnosis
for pemphigus vulgaris.

770
00:42:37,390 --> 00:42:40,170
And lastly, we'll
turn our attention to

771
00:42:40,170 --> 00:42:43,050
autoimmune diseases of
the vascular system.

772
00:42:44,230 --> 00:42:48,110
The first disease we'll mention
is immune thrombocytopenic

773
00:42:48,110 --> 00:42:50,730
purpura, in which case
you have autoantibodies

774
00:42:50,750 --> 00:42:55,630
against GP2B and 3A, and
these are both receptors in

775
00:42:55,630 --> 00:42:58,810
platelet aggregation, and
they stop the platelet plug

776
00:42:58,810 --> 00:43:01,610
essentially from forming.
And what we'll find is

777
00:43:01,610 --> 00:43:05,210
dysfunction in your blood and
platelets. So with the signs

778
00:43:05,210 --> 00:43:08,370
and symptoms, will have
purpura and mucocutaneous

779
00:43:08,370 --> 00:43:12,250
bleeding specifically because
of the platelet dysfunction

780
00:43:12,250 --> 00:43:15,230
and on top of that ultimately
you can have splenic

781
00:43:15,230 --> 00:43:18,230
destruction. Initially
you might see splenomegaly

782
00:43:18,230 --> 00:43:21,690
because the macrophages help
to phagocytose the platelets

783
00:43:21,690 --> 00:43:24,530
that are dysfunctional
leading to the splenomegaly

784
00:43:24,530 --> 00:43:28,350
and ultimately splenic
destruction and signs and symptoms

785
00:43:28,350 --> 00:43:31,330
and presentation are
commonly pallor and fatigue.

786
00:43:33,710 --> 00:43:37,510
In terms of diagnosis of
immune thrombocytopenic purpura

787
00:43:37,510 --> 00:43:41,090
we have specifically an
isolated thrombocytopenia

788
00:43:41,090 --> 00:43:44,170
or low platelet count and
it's predominantly a diagnosis

789
00:43:44,170 --> 00:43:46,750
of exclusion so much of
the testing that will be

790
00:43:46,750 --> 00:43:50,710
done is actually excluding
other diseases. For example

791
00:43:50,710 --> 00:43:53,170
you might do a blood smear
and see findings like

792
00:43:53,170 --> 00:43:55,650
schistocytes and that'll point
you more in the direction

793
00:43:55,650 --> 00:43:59,630
of TTP or hemolytic uremic
syndrome and other disease

794
00:43:59,630 --> 00:44:02,950
processes. In terms of the
treatment, it does somewhat

795
00:44:02,950 --> 00:44:05,930
vary based off of the
population of children or

796
00:44:05,930 --> 00:44:08,950
adults, and in children
it's really supportive care

797
00:44:08,950 --> 00:44:11,970
predominantly, but when we
get to adults, we do have

798
00:44:11,970 --> 00:44:16,130
corticosteroids, IVIG, and again
we're mentioning rituximab.

799
00:44:16,130 --> 00:44:18,990
In this case, rituximab
targets the B cells that

800
00:44:18,990 --> 00:44:21,730
are responsible for
producing the antibodies that

801
00:44:21,730 --> 00:44:25,070
destroy your platelets. So
rituxanab binds to the B cells

802
00:44:25,070 --> 00:44:27,490
to help your immune
system destroy the B cell,

803
00:44:27,490 --> 00:44:31,310
decreasing the overall burden
of the antibody production.

804
00:44:33,950 --> 00:44:37,270
And lastly, we'll be
discussing antiphospholipid

805
00:44:37,270 --> 00:44:40,130
syndrome. This might not be
a disease process that you

806
00:44:40,130 --> 00:44:42,930
commonly see. However, when
you're considering patients

807
00:44:42,930 --> 00:44:45,930
with recurrent thrombotic
events like spontaneous

808
00:44:45,930 --> 00:44:49,290
abortions, deep vein
thrombosis, pulmonary emboli,

809
00:44:49,290 --> 00:44:52,530
this does become a big
differential to consider in

810
00:44:52,530 --> 00:44:55,130
your patients who have
hypercoagulable conditions and

811
00:44:55,130 --> 00:44:58,750
hypercoagulable states.
So here it's an autoimmune

812
00:44:58,750 --> 00:45:01,870
disease specifically with
autoantibodies or antibodies

813
00:45:01,870 --> 00:45:05,250
to cardiolipin and lupus
anticoagulant and these

814
00:45:05,250 --> 00:45:07,750
react against the proteins
that bind to the plasma

815
00:45:07,750 --> 00:45:12,070
membrane. So this can be
primary or secondary meaning on

816
00:45:12,070 --> 00:45:15,430
its own antiphospholipid
syndrome is a primary syndrome.

817
00:45:15,430 --> 00:45:17,690
However, you can also
find this in conjunction

818
00:45:17,690 --> 00:45:22,330
or along with lupus. Now,
it's not organ-specific. It

819
00:45:22,330 --> 00:45:25,330
is a hematologic consideration,
but can go across

820
00:45:25,330 --> 00:45:28,410
multiple body systems and
organ systems. There's a

821
00:45:28,410 --> 00:45:31,030
classification system on the
next slide that will tell

822
00:45:31,030 --> 00:45:33,770
you that really in more
than three body systems or

823
00:45:33,770 --> 00:45:37,010
organ systems involved, this
can become catastrophic.

824
00:45:37,210 --> 00:45:40,010
I mentioned again, these
patients will have recurrent

825
00:45:40,010 --> 00:45:42,490
thrombotic events,
deep pain thrombosis,

826
00:45:42,490 --> 00:45:46,450
spontaneous abortions, CVAs,
or myocardial infarctions.

827
00:45:46,450 --> 00:45:49,510
And furthermore, another
finding on skin exam

828
00:45:49,510 --> 00:45:52,230
you'll see, which is not
specific to this disease

829
00:45:52,230 --> 00:45:55,250
process, is levito
reticularis, which appears

830
00:45:55,250 --> 00:45:58,890
as mottled or lacy
reticular appearing skin.

831
00:46:00,250 --> 00:46:03,190
Now this process does
actually have its own

832
00:46:03,190 --> 00:46:05,650
classification criteria,
but what's important for

833
00:46:05,650 --> 00:46:08,750
you to know is we need
the positive findings

834
00:46:08,750 --> 00:46:12,930
of anticardiolipin,
IgG, or IgM, as well as

835
00:46:12,930 --> 00:46:15,770
positive lupus anticoagulant,
and you may also have

836
00:46:15,770 --> 00:46:18,610
findings positive for
beta-2 glycoprotein 1.

837
00:46:18,630 --> 00:46:21,250
On top of the lab
findings, you also have

838
00:46:21,250 --> 00:46:23,970
clinical findings of
vascular thromboses,

839
00:46:23,970 --> 00:46:25,790
pregnancy morbidities, and the

840
00:46:25,790 --> 00:46:27,350
recurrent thrombotic events.

841
00:46:27,870 --> 00:46:31,530
Because this is a hypercoagulable
state, the treatment

842
00:46:31,530 --> 00:46:34,910
is lifelong anticoagulation
with warfarin. Typically

843
00:46:34,910 --> 00:46:37,590
heparin is actually used
in pregnant patients.

844
00:46:39,830 --> 00:46:42,710
Now that we've discussed
antiphospholipid syndrome

845
00:46:42,710 --> 00:46:45,390
that does bring us to the
end of our lecture and end

846
00:46:45,390 --> 00:46:48,550
of our discussion. One thing
that I like to do and one

847
00:46:48,550 --> 00:46:51,030
thing that I think may
help in understanding the

848
00:46:51,030 --> 00:46:53,910
lecture and the content that
we had just discussed is

849
00:46:53,910 --> 00:46:57,350
coming up with a small chart
to consider the differences

850
00:46:57,350 --> 00:47:00,350
in each disease process.
The things that can

851
00:47:00,350 --> 00:47:03,590
become complicated are when
clinical presentation are

852
00:47:03,590 --> 00:47:06,270
often the same, but I
think making a chart of the

853
00:47:06,270 --> 00:47:08,650
different antibodies, the
clinical signs that might

854
00:47:08,650 --> 00:47:11,790
overlap or might distinguish
one from another, and also

855
00:47:11,790 --> 00:47:14,770
some of the histological
or pathological findings

856
00:47:14,770 --> 00:47:17,750
that you'd see are what's
going to be able to help you

857
00:47:17,750 --> 00:47:20,630
in distinguishing one
disease process from another.

858
00:47:24,370 --> 00:47:26,670
That being said, we are at the

859
00:47:26,670 --> 00:47:28,630
end of our lecture
and discussion.

